props.markdown:
These carry no information that isn't also available as text, in the tooltip or in the data table, so they keep their low contrast (WCAG 1.4.11 applies to what is needed to understand the content):

- grid lines and row dividers;
- bar, meter and inline-bar tracks, the bar of a `ShareBar` that has its list, and the tick labels of a `ZoneMeter` (the value text already names the zone);
- the light tint between hatch stripes, and the faded end of `hatch-fade` bars;
- soft dots (the faded non-peak periods in WaffleColumns): any dot drawn soft is decorative emphasis and gets no 3:1 outline;
- dimmed marks while another one is active;
- bands (a likely range), regions (forecast shading) and the column highlight;
- dotted connectors between waterfall steps;
- the dashed border of an empty heatmap cell, and the glow on its top cell.
